- Lucky?
 - Look at his shirt.

932
00:36:13,000 --> 00:36:14,137
You call this lucky?

933
00:36:17,068 --> 00:36:20,379
- Look, Mr. Wooster, my best
friend was buried this morning.

934
00:36:20,379 --> 00:36:22,137
Yesterday I lost my job.

935
00:36:22,137 --> 00:36:24,448
I can't drive a car for
a whole stinkin' year.

936
00:36:24,448 --> 00:36:26,000
- [Crow] Uh huh, and?

937
00:36:26,000 --> 00:36:27,724
- I'm sorry about
 the DeMarco kid.

938
00:36:27,724 --> 00:36:28,965
Close, huh?

939
00:36:28,965 --> 00:36:31,034
- Some guys have got brothers.

940
00:36:31,034 --> 00:36:32,000
I had Sonny.

941
00:36:32,000 --> 00:36:33,413
- Where are your folks, Phil?

942
00:36:33,413 --> 00:36:35,137
- I ran away when I was 14.

943
00:36:35,137 --> 00:36:38,068
The old man and old lady didn't
even bother to look for me.

944
00:36:38,068 --> 00:36:40,000
- Well, I'll let
 you in on something.

945
00:36:40,000 --> 00:36:41,310
I ran away when I was 15.

946
00:36:41,310 --> 00:36:42,551
- [Crow] Does that
 tell you anything?

947
00:36:42,551 --> 00:36:43,793
- So what?

948
00:36:43,793 --> 00:36:45,068
- I understand you
 work for a carnival?

949
00:36:45,068 --> 00:36:46,275
- Yeah.

950
00:36:46,275 --> 00:36:47,241
- [Tom] Yeah, I bit
the heads off chickens.

951
00:36:47,241 --> 00:36:48,862
- Daredevil driving act.

952
00:36:48,862 --> 00:36:51,551
