- [Tom] I need an operation.

1218
00:47:41,551 --> 00:47:43,448
- Hey, you know the rules
 about smoking in here.

1219
00:47:43,448 --> 00:47:46,586
Smoke of the cigar, it's
 like exotic perfume compared

1220
00:47:46,586 --> 00:47:48,172
with the air in here.

1221
00:47:50,275 --> 00:47:51,655
- [Crow] Hey, I'm in there.

1222
00:47:51,655 --> 00:47:53,137
Oh no, that's me here.

1223
00:47:53,137 --> 00:47:55,758
- [Tom] Let's see,
 jockstrap, another jockstrap.

1224
00:47:55,758 --> 00:47:56,655
- Nothin' yet.
This guy really

1225
00:47:56,655 --> 00:47:57,482
liked jockstraps.

1226
00:47:59,206 --> 00:48:01,000
- Wait a minute.

1227
00:48:01,000 --> 00:48:02,586
- [Crow] It's my brain.

1228
00:48:02,586 --> 00:48:03,413
Found it.

1229
00:48:05,034 --> 00:48:07,103
- [Chillis] Well, the
joke's on me, isn't it?

1230
00:48:07,103 --> 00:48:09,000
- You think nobody
 has a brain, but you.

1231
00:48:09,000 --> 00:48:10,724
- Quite to the contrary, Bruce.

1232
00:48:10,724 --> 00:48:13,620
I'm the first to bow
 to superior intellect.

1233
00:48:13,620 --> 00:48:16,206
It's just that I very rarely
 encounter it. [laughs]

1234
00:48:16,206 --> 00:48:18,206
- [Tom] Well, you Schneidered
 me on that one boss.

1235
00:48:18,206 --> 00:48:19,413
You shaved ol' Bruce.

1236
00:48:19,413 --> 00:48:21,448
[Bruce] Hold it, I
 wanna get that shower.

1237
00:48:22,413 --> 00:48:23,655
- [Chillis] Make it fast.

1238
00:48:23,655 --> 00:48:25,517
I can't stand the odor
 in here much longer.

1239
00:48:30,689 --> 00:48:32,103
Want the lights?
- Yeah.

1240
00:48:32,103 --> 00:48:34,448
- [Tom] Would you
 scratch my ear.

1241
00:48:34,448 --> 00:48:36,965
- [Bruce] Nevermind, I got it.
 - [Chillis] I guess with you,

1242
00:48:36,965 --> 00:48:38,379
it doesn't make any difference.

1243
00:48:38,379 --> 00:48:41,172
You can probably see
 just as well in the dark.

1244
00:48:41,172 --> 00:48:42,758
- [Crow] Yep, got
 me again, boss.

1245
00:48:42,758 --> 00:48:43,586
Yep, you did.

1246
00:48:45,413 --> 00:48:48,310
- [Joel] Hey, let's shower in
 our clothes just for a Lark.

1247
00:48:50,655 --> 00:48:52,931
[Crow] Geez, it smells
 like a locker room.

1248
00:48:52,931 --> 00:48:53,758
Oh, it is.

1249
00:48:54,689 --> 00:48:57,448
[dramatic music]

1250
00:49:02,448 --> 00:49:04,344
- [Tom] A teddy, a
 jock, a side of beef,

1251
00:49:04,344 --> 00:49:06,379
Annette Funicello poster?

1252
00:49:06,379 --> 00:49:07,931
Edgar Allen Poe poetry.

1253
00:49:09,103 --> 00:49:11,862
- [Crow] Oh no, he
 died of jock itch.

1254
00:49:11,862 --> 00:49:13,448
- Whatever it was, we missed it.

1255
00:49:20,655 --> 00:49:22,310
- [Tom] Return to Papyon.

1256
00:49:26,000 --> 00:49:27,620
- [Crow] A surgeon
 general warning.

1257
00:49:27,620 --> 00:49:29,586
- [Tom] Hey that's
 from Catalina Caper.

1258
00:49:33,206 --> 00:49:34,689
- [Joel] This is great.

1259
00:49:34,689 --> 00:49:36,344
We're having an adventure,
 just like the Goonies.

1260
00:49:38,000 --> 00:49:40,517
- I wish we knew what they
 took out of that locker.

1261
00:49:40,517 --> 00:49:42,896
- Maybe if we knew that,
 we'd know why Sonny's dead.

1262
00:49:42,896 --> 00:49:44,758
- You think they're the ones?

1263
00:49:44,758 --> 00:49:46,172
- I don't know.

1264
00:49:46,172 --> 00:49:47,655
I don't know.

1265
00:49:47,655 --> 00:49:50,551
But ever since he joined this
 gym, he seemed to change.

1266
00:49:50,551 --> 00:49:52,655
- Yeah, he got bulkier.
- Changed how?

1267
00:49:52,655 --> 00:49:54,068
- Well, he had
 something on his mind.

1268
00:49:54,068 --> 00:49:55,448
- Water.
 - Somethin' that was

1269
00:49:55,448 --> 00:49:57,310
really buggin' him.

1270
00:49:57,310 --> 00:50:00,034
Whenever I'd ask him
about it, he'd clam up.

1271
00:50:00,034 --> 00:50:01,482
- Maybe it was
 because of his mother.

1272
00:50:01,482 --> 00:50:03,241
- [Tom] Hey, his
 mother was a Saint.

1273
00:50:03,241 --> 00:50:04,655
- That's what I figured too.

1274
00:50:05,827 --> 00:50:07,482
But now.

1275
00:50:07,482 --> 00:50:08,896
- [Tom] Yeah?

1276
00:50:08,896 --> 00:50:09,724
- [Phil] I wonder.

1277
00:50:09,724 --> 00:50:11,172
- What, what?

1278
00:50:11,172 --> 00:50:12,827
- [Crow] Hey, put on
Dude Looks Like a Lady.

1279
00:50:12,827 --> 00:50:13,689
I love that.

1280
00:50:17,758 --> 00:50:20,379
All right, I'll have the pork
 rind ball to lie down with

1281
00:50:20,379 --> 00:50:22,827
and a diet Coke, please.

1282
00:50:22,827 --> 00:50:24,413
- Did you ask him?

1283
00:50:24,413 --> 00:50:25,896
- Ask who what?

1284
00:50:25,896 --> 00:50:28,379
- Ask Barney about
 a job, what else?

1285
00:50:28,379 --> 00:50:29,724
- No.

1286
00:50:29,724 --> 00:50:31,068
- Well, let's try now.

1287
00:50:31,068 --> 00:50:33,103
Hey, Barney.
 - Google.

1288
00:50:33,103 --> 00:50:35,758
- Barney, how'd you like
to double your business?

1289
00:50:35,758 --> 00:50:37,793
- No thanks.
 - What's the joke?

1290
00:50:37,793 --> 00:50:39,068
- No joke.

1291
00:50:39,068 --> 00:50:40,931
All you have to do
 is hire Phil here,

1292
00:50:40,931 --> 00:50:43,344
and I'll personally guarantee
 that within a month's time,

1293
00:50:43,344 --> 00:50:45,482
your business'll be doubled.

1294
00:50:45,482 --> 00:50:46,448
- Hire him as what?

1295
00:50:46,448 --> 00:50:48,517
- Well, as a singer, what else?

1296
00:50:48,517 --> 00:50:50,862
- He's lucky I let
 him in here to sing.

1297
00:50:50,862 --> 00:50:52,965
- Don't worry, laughin'
 boy, it won't happen again.

1298
00:50:52,965 --> 00:50:54,000
- Take it easy, Phil.

1299
00:50:55,241 --> 00:50:56,689
- Forget it.

1300
00:50:56,689 --> 00:50:57,517
- Excuse me.

1301
00:50:58,448 --> 00:50:59,413
I'm Sydney Chillis.

1302
00:50:59,413 --> 00:51:01,000
I'd like to talk with you.

1303
00:51:01,000 --> 00:51:02,586
May I buy you a drink?

1304
00:51:02,586 --> 00:51:03,931
- I'm in a hurry, Mac.

1305
00:51:03,931 --> 00:51:06,413
- It might be worth your while.

1306
00:51:06,413 --> 00:51:08,379
- [Crow] A clue, a clue, a clue.

1307
00:51:11,137 --> 00:51:14,310
That's a clue.
 - Yeah.

1308
00:51:14,310 --> 00:51:17,206
- [Crow] Wow, I'm my own
Saturday night thing.

1309
00:51:17,206 --> 00:51:19,068
- [Tom] It's a
 drive-up stud service.

1310
00:51:21,344 --> 00:51:22,344
- You Phil Sandifer?

1311
00:51:23,206 --> 00:51:25,034
- [Crow] You Lou Reed?

1312
00:51:25,034 --> 00:51:26,068
- Yeah, that's right.

1313
00:51:27,241 --> 00:51:30,344
- Marsha Hay, Mr.
 Chillis' manicurist.

1314
00:51:36,758 --> 00:51:37,724
- [Tom] It's real.

1315
00:51:37,724 --> 00:51:38,965
I've seen these, they're nice.

1316
00:51:38,965 --> 00:51:40,241
You're a lucky woman.

1317
00:51:40,241 --> 00:51:42,413
- I guess he must
 pay pretty well.

1318
00:51:42,413 --> 00:51:44,000
- It's not mine.

1319
00:51:44,000 --> 00:51:45,793
Belongs to Mr. Chillis.

1320
00:51:45,793 --> 00:51:47,275
He lets me use it for errands.

1321
00:51:48,689 --> 00:51:50,068
Get in.

1322
00:51:50,068 --> 00:51:51,689
- [Joel] Wanted, manicurist
 for an evil slob.

1323
00:51:51,689 --> 00:51:53,137
- All righty.
- Photo a must.

1324
00:51:57,000 --> 00:51:58,551
- [Tom] Ooh, these
 seats are hot.

1325
00:51:58,551 --> 00:52:00,379
- So you're the new singer.

1326
00:52:00,379 --> 00:52:02,310
- [Crow] Yep, Isaac
 Basher, the singer.

1327
00:52:02,310 --> 00:52:03,586
- I didn't say I'd take it yet.

1328
00:52:05,310 --> 00:52:06,620
- I hope you do.

1329
00:52:06,620 --> 00:52:09,413
- [Joel] Because I want
you to go on and on.

1330
00:52:10,758 --> 00:52:12,379
- [Crow] They make
 love on the highways.

1331
00:52:12,379 --> 00:52:13,310
Love on the byways.

1332
00:52:13,310 --> 00:52:16,275
Love in the streets. [laughs]

1333
00:52:17,413 --> 00:52:20,448
[swanky music]

1334
00:52:20,448 --> 00:52:22,586
- [Crow] Boy, they went all
 out for this grand opening.

1335
00:52:22,586 --> 00:52:24,793
- [Joel] See, you put one
 foot in front of the other

1336
00:52:24,793 --> 00:52:27,310
and then you're
 walking in the door.

1337
00:52:27,310 --> 00:52:28,758
- I call 'em stairs.
 - Yeah.

1338
00:52:29,965 --> 00:52:31,310
- [Tom] Now I know
 this is bad luck,

1339
00:52:31,310 --> 00:52:32,931
but you're already in the movie.

1340
00:52:36,551 --> 00:52:38,344
- This'll all be finished
 by tomorrow night.

1341
00:52:39,517 --> 00:52:40,482
Wait here a second.

1342
00:52:43,862 --> 00:52:45,965
- Beetle Bailey,
 what's he up to now?

1343
00:52:45,965 --> 00:52:46,965
- Bring the singer?

1344
00:52:46,965 --> 00:52:48,034
- Yeah, where's Sydney.

1345
00:52:48,034 --> 00:52:49,827
- Where do you think?

1346
00:52:49,827 --> 00:52:50,862
- All right to go in?

1347
00:52:50,862 --> 00:52:51,827
- You modest?

1348
00:52:51,827 --> 00:52:53,103
- [Crow] What do you think?

1349
00:52:55,689 --> 00:52:57,068
- Sydney, singer's here.

1350
00:52:58,551 --> 00:53:00,137
- [Crow] What, are they
 in a double-wide trailer?

1351
00:53:02,413 --> 00:53:03,655
- [Tom] Hi, still here.

1352
00:53:07,206 --> 00:53:08,344
- Get him outta here.

1353
00:53:08,344 --> 00:53:10,034
- Toga, toga.
 - Get him outta here.

1354
00:53:10,034 --> 00:53:12,275
- Toga, toga.
 - Calm down.

1355
00:53:12,275 --> 00:53:13,965
He's having one of his fits.
 What on earth is wrong?

1356
00:53:13,965 --> 00:53:15,482
- That kid out there,
he's the one who come in

1357
00:53:15,482 --> 00:53:16,965
about DeMarco's locker.

1358
00:53:16,965 --> 00:53:18,413
- So?
 - But he had the key.

1359
00:53:18,413 --> 00:53:19,655
Maybe he knew-

1360
00:53:19,655 --> 00:53:21,000
- Come over here and
 start on my back.

1361
00:53:21,000 --> 00:53:23,034
- [Tom] And get me my
 Filipino house boy.

1362
00:53:29,965 --> 00:53:32,551
- Now, Bruce, you don't
think for a minute

1363
00:53:32,551 --> 00:53:34,758
I'd blunder
 haphazardly into this.

1364
00:53:36,000 --> 00:53:38,517
I've done some
 checking on this boy.

1365
00:53:38,517 --> 00:53:41,793
He was a friend of Leonard's,
 a very close friend.

1366
00:53:41,793 --> 00:53:44,379
So you see, it's only natural
 he'd want to clean out

1367
00:53:44,379 --> 00:53:45,620
the boy's locker.

1368
00:53:45,620 --> 00:53:47,413
- Yeah, but suppose
 he sees me here.

1369
00:53:47,413 --> 00:53:48,655
- He's going to see you.

1370
00:53:49,896 --> 00:53:51,931
- But he'll get wise to every-
 - Keep working.

1371
00:53:51,931 --> 00:53:54,275
You've over-stimulated
 your heart.

1372
00:53:54,275 --> 00:53:55,310
- And grossed us all out.
 - I don't want you

1373
00:53:55,310 --> 00:53:56,137
standing around.

1374
00:53:57,448 --> 00:53:59,724
You're my personal masseur.

1375
00:53:59,724 --> 00:54:02,344
Who's a more logical
 candidate for that position,

1376
00:54:02,344 --> 00:54:04,137
but a gym manager.

1377
00:54:04,137 --> 00:54:07,724
And suppose, just
 suppose he is suspicious.

1378
00:54:07,724 --> 00:54:09,793
What a better place to
have him than right here

1379
00:54:09,793 --> 00:54:10,965
under our noses.

1380
00:54:12,344 --> 00:54:16,310
Easy, Bruce, your little
 tantrum was all for nothing.

1381
00:54:16,310 --> 00:54:17,862
- [Tom] He's basting in butter.

1382
00:54:19,517 --> 00:54:21,103
- [Bruce] It's okay,
 he's your responsibility.

1383
00:54:21,103 --> 00:54:23,034
- Of course he's
 my responsibility.

1384
00:54:24,206 --> 00:54:25,137
- [Joel] I promise to
 feed him twice a day

1385
00:54:25,137 --> 00:54:26,413
and take him for walks.

1386
00:54:26,413 --> 00:54:27,206
- Unless we have someone
to make the deliveries,

1387
00:54:27,206 --> 00:54:28,758
we're out of business.

1388
00:54:28,758 --> 00:54:31,000
Unfortunately I don't have
 the stomach for that sort of

1389
00:54:31,000 --> 00:54:33,551
thing, and you
 don't have the eyes.

1390
00:54:33,551 --> 00:54:35,068
- [Crow] You got me.

1391
00:54:35,068 --> 00:54:37,379
- Bruce, let's be honest.

1392
00:54:37,379 --> 00:54:38,620
- This movie sucks.
 - Neither of us

1393
00:54:38,620 --> 00:54:40,206
can carry a tune. [laughs]

1394
00:54:40,206 --> 00:54:41,517
- [Tom] Oh yeah, that too.

1395
00:54:43,137 --> 00:54:44,000
- Okay, handsome.

1396
00:54:45,000 --> 00:54:46,241
- Okay.

1397
00:54:46,241 --> 00:54:47,896
- You smell like
 Captain Kangaroo.

1398
00:54:49,862 --> 00:54:52,793
- [Joel] Come in, Jedidiah,
pour yourself some Paul Masson.

1399
00:54:52,793 --> 00:54:54,413
- Sorry to keep you
 waiting, Philip.

1400
00:54:54,413 --> 00:54:56,827
I was in the middle
 of a steam bath.

1401
00:54:56,827 --> 00:54:58,000
- That's all right.

1402
00:54:58,000 --> 00:55:00,310
- No it's not, it's
 downright rude.

1403
00:55:00,310 --> 00:55:01,620
I hope you will forgive me.

1404
00:55:03,448 --> 00:55:04,931
Now let's see.

1405
00:55:04,931 --> 00:55:06,448
You know Marsha.

1406
00:55:06,448 --> 00:55:08,586
The gentlemen on the chair
 is Mr. Green, my masseur.

1407
00:55:08,586 --> 00:55:09,413
- We've met.

1408
00:55:10,862 --> 00:55:11,689
- Oh, you have?

1409
00:55:16,482 --> 00:55:18,862
- You're the one who came in
about the DeMarco kid's locker.

1410
00:55:18,862 --> 00:55:20,137
- [Tom] Yeah, and you're
 the one who can't see beyond

1411
00:55:20,137 --> 00:55:21,793
his nose.
 - That's right, I'm the one.

1412
00:55:21,793 --> 00:55:23,310
- Friend of his was
 enrolled in the gym.

1413
00:55:23,310 --> 00:55:25,206
Doin' real fine too.

1414
00:55:25,206 --> 00:55:26,551
Had an auto accident.

1415
00:55:26,551 --> 00:55:29,344
- I certainly hope it
wasn't anything serious.

1416
00:55:29,344 --> 00:55:30,482
- He died.

1417
00:55:30,482 --> 00:55:32,000
- My condolences.

1418
00:55:32,000 --> 00:55:33,827
What can you say in a
 situation like this?

1419
00:55:33,827 --> 00:55:35,620
Words are so meaningless.

1420
00:55:35,620 --> 00:55:36,862
- [Crow] I'd like to
 say a really bad joke.

1421
00:55:36,862 --> 00:55:38,793
- Well, what do you
 think of my club?

1422
00:55:38,793 --> 00:55:40,379
- [Crow] Foot.

1423
00:55:40,379 --> 00:55:42,448
- I think it's very nice.

1424
00:55:42,448 --> 00:55:44,965
- I put in a great
 deal of thought into
 making the High Note

1425
00:55:44,965 --> 00:55:47,034
an inducement for our
 young people to gather

1426
00:55:47,034 --> 00:55:49,379
for wholesome fun and music.

1427
00:55:49,379 --> 00:55:51,620
- And evil.
- Now look, Mr. Chillis.

1428
00:55:51,620 --> 00:55:52,862
You know my problem.

1429
00:55:52,862 --> 00:55:55,344
I'm on probation,
 no driver's license.

1430
00:55:55,344 --> 00:55:58,241
I explained that last night.

1431
00:55:58,241 --> 00:56:00,068
- Indeed, you did.

1432
00:56:00,068 --> 00:56:03,206
Just, as I promised, I've
 come up with a solution.

1433
00:56:03,206 --> 00:56:05,931
- [Joel] And we'll inject
 it straight into your head.

1434
00:56:05,931 --> 00:56:07,931
- I've got something
interesting to show you.

1435
00:56:07,931 --> 00:56:09,586
- [Tom] Something festive.

1436
00:56:09,586 --> 00:56:10,517
- [Chillis] Come along.

1437
00:56:11,965 --> 00:56:13,206
- [Tom] Yeah, we're meeting
 Peter Lawford for dinner.

1438
00:56:13,206 --> 00:56:15,482
- The bartender at
 the Rainbow Gardens,

1439
00:56:15,482 --> 00:56:19,206
he told me you've earned all
 kinds of honors racing cars.

1440
00:56:19,206 --> 00:56:20,931
- Well yeah, I won a few drags.

1441
00:56:20,931 --> 00:56:22,586
- That's why I think you'll
 appreciate what I have

1442
00:56:22,586 --> 00:56:23,413
to show you.

1443
00:56:25,413 --> 00:56:27,206
Well, what do you think of it?

1444
00:56:27,206 --> 00:56:29,482
- [Joel] It's a tiny
statue of Saint Francis.

1445
00:56:29,482 --> 00:56:30,413
- You're kiddin'?

1446
00:56:31,586 --> 00:56:33,586
- Wait, my boy, never
 jump at conclusions.

1447
00:56:33,586 --> 00:56:34,931
Open the hood.

1448
00:56:34,931 --> 00:56:35,758
Go ahead.

1449
00:56:38,275 --> 00:56:43,172
- Oh my God!
 - Oh that's terrible!

1450
00:56:43,172 --> 00:56:44,655
- An espresso machine?
 - That's fantastic!

1451
00:56:44,655 --> 00:56:47,275
- Well, a house like this
 needs expert driving.

1452
00:56:48,379 --> 00:56:49,965
- Wanna bet I could handle her?

1453
00:56:50,931 --> 00:56:52,379
- I'm sure you could.

1454
00:56:52,379 --> 00:56:54,137
- [Tom] Have you ever
 thought about being evil?

1455
00:56:54,137 --> 00:56:55,310
I mean really evil?

1456
00:56:56,689 --> 00:56:57,931
- Oh, what's the
use Mr. Chillis?

1457
00:56:57,931 --> 00:57:00,206
Why are we even talkin'
about a job out here?

1458
00:57:01,551 --> 00:57:03,172
